    "tarball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/VebjornNyvoll/automate-net-combat/tarball/v0.1.5",
    "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/VebjornNyvoll/automate-net-combat/zipball/v0.1.5",
    "body": "## Bug fix\n\nThe Black ICE actor sheet showed \"n/a\" for damage formula because the linked program was embedded as an owned item, but CPR's sheet looks up programs via `game.items.filter(i => i.uuid === programUUID)` — embedded items aren't visible there.\n\n## Match the canonical CPR pattern\n\nStudied `cpr-cyberdeck.js#_rezBlackIceToken` and `cpr-black-ice-sheet.js#_configureFromProgram` to align with how the system itself spawns Black ICE:\n\n- **One shared world-level program per Black ICE key**, organized in a `Black ICE Programs (auto)` folder. Multiple actors of the same type share the template; each actor carries its own REZ pool, so HP isn't shared.\n- **Token flags** match the CPR contract: `programUUID`, `sceneId`, and `netrunnerTokenId` when the target's token is on the scene. The sheet's `getData()` and the sync-with-program hook both expect these.\n- **Reverse-link** on the program (`biTokenId` + `sceneId` on the `cyberpunk-red-core` flag namespace) so the system can find the spawned token from the program side too.\n- **Lifecycle**: deleting a Black ICE actor clears the program's reverse flags but doesn't delete the shared template.\n\nThe damage formula now resolves on the sheet, and Configure From Program lists the auto-imported templates correctly."
  },
