    "body": "## Bug fix: target picker now works\n\nThe v0.1.0 canvas-click netrunner picker was unreliable — token placeables consume PIXI pointer events before our stage-level handler runs, so the picker silently no-op'd in many setups.\n\n**Fix:** Replaced canvas-click target picking with dialog-driven scene-token pickers.\n\n- New \\`pickNetrunnerFromScene\\`: lists tokens on the active scene whose actor has a Netrunner role item (or, as fallback, a cyberdeck). Auto-resolves if exactly one match; otherwise shows a dropdown dialog.\n- Same dialog pattern reused for attack-target fallback when a Black ICE has no flagged target.\n- Multi-netrunner parties now resolve cleanly via the dropdown.\n\n### Updating\n\nFoundry will offer the update automatically next time it polls. Or pull manually via the manifest URL:\n\n\\`\\`\\`\nhttps://github.com/VebjornNyvoll/automate-net-combat/releases/latest/download/module.json\n\\`\\`\\`"
  },
